{
  "id": "r22_refrigerant___properties",
  "title": "R22 Refrigerant - Properties",
  "description": "Properties of Refrigerant R22 Dichlorodifluoromethane - saturated liquid and saturated vapor - imperial and metric units. R22 is a single HydroChloroFluoroCarbon (HCFC) compound with ODP=0.05 and GWP=1700.",
  "type": "calculator-table",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "# R22 Refrigerant - Properties\n\nProperties of Refrigerant R22 Dichlorodifluoromethane - saturated liquid and saturated vapor.\n\nR22 is a single HydroChloroFluoroCarbon (HCFC) compound. It has low chlorine content and ozone depletion potential (ODP = 0.05) and a modest global warming potential (GWP = 1700).\n\nR22 can be used in small heat pump systems, but new systems cannot be manufactured for use in the EU after 2003. From 2010 only recycled or saved stocks of R22 can be used."
    },
